## TROUBLESHOOTING QUESTIONS

---

**Q17. TROUBLESHOOTING: A StatefulSet is stuck at `READY: 1/3`. `web-0` is Running, but `web-1` never starts. What do you check?**

With `OrderedReady` policy, `web-1` will NOT start until `web-0` is
Running AND Ready. "Running" (the container process started) and
"Ready" (readiness probe passing) are DIFFERENT states. If `web-0`
shows `STATUS: Running` but `READY: 0/1`, its readiness probe is
failing — and the StatefulSet controller is BLOCKING on it,
preventing `web-1` from ever being created.

```bash
# Step 1 -- check individual pod readiness
kubectl get pods -l app=<name>
# web-0 might show 0/1 Ready even though STATUS is Running

# Step 2 -- check why web-0's readiness probe is failing
kubectl describe pod web-0
# Look at Events section for "Readiness probe failed: ..."

# Step 3 -- test the readiness endpoint directly
kubectl exec web-0 -- curl -v localhost:<port>/ready

# Step 4 -- check pod logs
kubectl logs web-0
```

Fix the readiness probe issue on `web-0` (or increase
`initialDelaySeconds` if the app just needs more warm-up time), and
once `web-0` becomes Ready, the StatefulSet controller will
automatically proceed to create `web-1`.

