**Q20. TROUBLESHOOTING: You run `kubectl scale sts postgres --replicas=5`. After a few minutes, you only see 4 pods instead of 5. `kubectl get sts postgres` shows `DESIRED: 5, CURRENT: 4`. What do you investigate?**

With `OrderedReady`, the StatefulSet controller is trying to create
`postgres-4`, but something is preventing it from becoming Ready,
so the total count is stuck at 4 (existing) rather than 5 (desired).

```bash
# Step 1 -- check if the pod was created at all
kubectl get pods -l app=postgres
# If postgres-4 exists but is Pending/CrashLoopBackOff, it was
# created but can't become Ready

# Step 2 -- describe the new pod
kubectl describe pod postgres-4

# Step 3 -- check if the PVC was created and bound
kubectl get pvc data-postgres-4
# If it shows Pending (not Bound), no storage is available --
# check StorageClass and if your cloud has EBS volume capacity

# Common causes:
# - PVC stuck Pending (StorageClass misconfigured, cloud quota exceeded)
# - New pod stuck Pending (node resources insufficient)
# - New pod CrashLoopBackOff (app error on this new replica)
# - Readiness probe failing on new pod (blocking controller from
#   marking it Ready and proceeding)
```

